# Nano live desktop environments: the only supported sessions in the Nano ISO.
# Both sessions are installed side-by-side and exposed by SDDM at login.
# LXQt (Qt desktop; lightweight X11 session).
lxqt-about
lxqt-admin
lxqt-archiver
lxqt-config
lxqt-globalkeys
lxqt-notificationd
lxqt-openssh-askpass
lxqt-panel
lxqt-policykit
lxqt-powermanagement
lxqt-qtplugin
lxqt-runner
lxqt-session
lxqt-sudo
lxqt-themes
pcmanfm-qt
udisks2
gvfs
gvfs-mtp
gvfs-smb
qterminal
openbox
pavucontrol-qt
lximage-qt
screengrab
qps

# MATE (traditional GTK desktop).
caja
caja-image-converter
caja-share
engrampa
eom
mate-control-center
mate-desktop
mate-icon-theme
mate-media
mate-menus
mate-notification-daemon
mate-panel
mate-polkit
mate-power-manager
mate-screensaver
mate-session-manager
mate-settings-daemon
mate-terminal
marco
mozo
atril
pluma

# Shared display manager, X11 compatibility, Qt and GTK integration.
sddm
xorg-server
xorg-xwayland
qt5-wayland
qt6-wayland
gtk3
noto-fonts
noto-fonts-emoji
ttf-dejavu
ttf-liberation
gnome-keyring
polkit
network-manager-applet
nm-connection-editor
xdg-user-dirs
xdg-utils

# Nexora welcome and document tools; omit nexora-desktop because its meta-package
# pulls in Halcyon. Nano's only desktop sessions are LXQt and MATE.
@DISTRO_ID@-welcome
@DISTRO_ID@-write
